  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u01-1",
      "title": "One to five",
      "explanation": [
        "We start with numbers: short, useful words that also teach you most Afrikaans sounds.",
        "**een** (1): the **ee** glides, like \"ee-uh\".",
        "**twee** (2): after a consonant, **w** sounds like English *w*.",
        "**drie** (3): **ie** sounds like *ee* in *see*, and the **r** is rolled.",
        "**vier** (4): **v** usually sounds like English *f*.",
        "**vyf** (5): **y** sounds like *ay* in *say*."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "een, twee, drie",
          "en": "one, two, three"
        },
        {
          "af": "vier, vyf",
          "en": "four, five"
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "een",
        "twee",
        "drie",
        "vier",
        "vyf"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "What is **drie**?",
          "options": [
            "3",
            "2",
            "5"
          ],
          "answer": "3"
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "How do you say 5?",
          "options": [
            "vyf",
            "vier",
            "twee"
          ],
          "answer": "vyf"
        },
        {
          "type": "fill",
          "af": "een, twee, ___, vier",
          "en": "one, two, …, four",
          "answers": [
            "drie"
          ],
          "options": [
            "drie",
            "vyf",
            "een"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "en",
          "prompt": "four",
          "answers": [
            "vier"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "af",
          "prompt": "twee",
          "answers": [
            "two",
            "2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "fill",
          "af": "twee + twee = ___",
          "en": "2 + 2 = ?",
          "answers": [
            "vier"
          ],
          "options": [
            "vier",
            "vyf",
            "drie"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "The **v** in **vyf** sounds like English…",
          "options": [
            "f",
            "v",
            "w"
          ],
          "answer": "f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u01-2",
      "title": "Six to ten",
      "explanation": [
        "**ses** (6).",
        "**sewe** (7): a **w** between vowels sounds like a soft *v*.",
        "**agt** (8): **g** is a throaty sound, like *ch* in Scottish *loch*. Afrikaans **g** almost always sounds like this.",
        "**nege** (9): two syllables, *nee-uh-khuh*.",
        "**tien** (10): like English *teen*."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "ses, sewe, agt",
          "en": "six, seven, eight"
        },
        {
          "af": "nege, tien",
          "en": "nine, ten"
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "ses",
        "sewe",
        "agt",
        "nege",
        "tien"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "What is **agt**?",
          "options": [
            "8",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
